    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nUpdated `DetermineRegistrationDate.java` so the business-day rule also rolls past public holidays:\n\n- Added a fixed `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set: `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`.\n- Rewrote `toBusinessDay` as a roll-forward loop that advances one day at a time while the date is a weekend **or** a listed holiday. A single-step check wasn't enough here \u2014 e.g. Fri 2026-12-25 (holiday) \u2192 Sat 26 (weekend) \u2192 Sun 27 (weekend) \u2192 Mon 28 (holiday) \u2192 Tue 29 \u2014 so the loop is necessary to skip consecutive weekend/holiday runs.\n- Refactored the weekend check into an `isWeekend` helper and updated the class Javadoc.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test asserts the black-box invariant (default registrationDate never a Saturday/Sunday), which still holds; the specific holiday calendar is enforced by the implementation directly since the server clock/calendar can't be driven black-box.",
